speechtext:
There is a revote of $20,000. The details are as follows:
(1)	To complete the contract with Messrs Henry and Ross for the reconstruction m concrete of 174 feet of the superstructure of the south pier and 300 feet of the north pier, $15,800; . . ,
(2)	Towards the reconstruction ot two lur-ther sections of the north pier, 100 feet long and 200 feet long, respectively, the former section requiring to be completely removed by dredging. Allotment for 1928-29, $17,200;
(3)	To dredge entrance channel to , depth of 20 feet, a total distance of 1,490 feet, 20,000 cubic yards at 45 cents, $9,000;
(4)	General repairs to harbour works, $1,000.
That makes a total of $43,000.
